			<div class="content" id="post-content-4850340">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This doesn't have enough 'conflict' driving the story forwards: everyone feels like a passive observer at best, and there's not really anything pulling this forwards. It doesn't help that the various elements feel&#8230;disconnected?</p>
<p>Like, the exploration log doesn't smoothly lead into the interview because there's nothing really tying the exploration into the idea of the division between two church groups and that whole conflict; the two things feel completely separate thematically, particularly since the role of the snake and the yurt and stuff is just&#8230;completely irrelevant to the interview with -1 and the discovery that there's some spooky churches behind this and there's like&#8230;two sets of people and stuff? It feels like this just, doesn't tie all the elements involved in this together well enough, or do much with anything and it's underwhelming as a result.</p>
<p>I would strongly suggest trimming down the concept: figure out what stuff is actually necessary, and get rid of all the unnecessary anomalous stuff. Like, you have this dude who's meant to be able to shape earth but that never actually comes up in this, so cut that aspect. You have the giant snake, but it's not really a major element so cut it from the description. You have the dude manifesting anomalies and talk of this spreading further, but none of that comes up so cut it. Be ruthless: anything that does not serve either the characterisation, the narrative or the emotional response here is unnecessary. Equally: any narrative thread that doesn't go anywhere is unnecessary; any characterisation that isn't purposeful is unnecessary.</p>
<p>This, at it's core, needs a central thing holding it up: an idea, or a theme; and it needs to figure out how to introduce that theme early and expand on it, and explore it throughout. Everything should serve the central core of this: the exploration should introduce it, the interview should expand it, and the note at the end should resolve it.</p>
<p>In it's current state, I would downvote this. I&#8230;am not confident that a version of this exists that I would upvote without you effectively starting from scratch on a more streamlined article.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><em>Gonna note that I can miss stuff; flag things which are right as being wrong and indeed flag things which are deliberately wrong.</em><br />
<em>I'll likely use <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">strikethrough</span> to indicate stuff to remove and <span style="color: green">green text</span> to indicate stuff to add.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>is to be kept in a standard humanoid cell <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">and it</span><span style="color: green">which</span> should be suspended in mid-air</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>with height measuring 300m from the sea level</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this phrasing implies exactly 300m; &quot;at least 300m above&quot; would be clearer than &quot;with height measuring 300m from&quot;</p>
<p>It feels to me like measuring it from sea level is a mistake: you want to convey that it's 300m from the ground, which isn't necessarily sea level.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Four wires are to be installed on all four sides to keep the cell stable.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think the exact details of the suspension can be elided; with the sole exception being if we need to understand this to know how a containment breach or something occurred.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is to be noted that all carbon-based life <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">are</span><span style="color: green">is</span> prohibited <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">to enter</span><span style="color: green">from entering</span> SCP-XXXX-1’s containment cell.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'carbon-based life' feels clunky here; I feel like 'personnel' is sufficient but?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a containment cell under equivalent containment procedures <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">as</span><span style="color: green">to</span> SCP-XXXX-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>A maximum of five hazmat-protected personnel <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">is</span><span style="color: green">are</span> permitted to enter SCP-XXXX at any given time.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Five personnel is plural; so are instead of is.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>all on-site personnel <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">is</span><span style="color: green">are</span> to evacuate or shelter in place until MTF-Theta-4 (&quot;Gardeners&quot;) apprehend SCP-XXXX-1 and its anomalies manifestation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think you want 'anomalous manifestations' here?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Description:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd get rid of the horizontal line immediately after this; though tbh, I'd generally lean to keeping the description and the first sentence of the description on the same line.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX consists of two interrelated anomalies: a cave, designated as SCP-XXXX</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is janky: you can't assign 'SCP-XXXX' to both 'the overall' and 'the cave' like this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the abandoned Mining facility</p>
</blockquote>
<p>mining shouldn't be capitalised here or anywhere in sentences like this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>in Tavan Bogd, Mongolia</p>
</blockquote>
<p>in the ConProcs, you refer to it as &quot;located in Altai Tavan Bogd, Mongolia&quot;; and it feels like you should be consistent here?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>it is measured to be around 6 kilometers deep.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's unclear whether this refers to the cave or the mine; I'd move the measurement depending on which:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is a 6km deep cave under the abandoned mining facility in Tavan Bogd, Mongolia.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>or:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is a cave under the 6km deep abandoned mining facility in Tavan Bogd, Mongolia.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This also prevents the kinda janky two clauses joined by a comma structure.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>at least one kilometer in length, that resides within the cave</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this feels really big in relation to the cave depth but? I guess it works if the cave is largely horizontal rather than vertical? It might be worth specifying an area the cave system takes up</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Within SCP-XXXX are groups of humanoid entities stationary in place, their physical traits are as same as humans but is made out of a roots that is growing a different species of flowers, those flowers are identical to the organism above the surface and is emitting unknown amount of pollen.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a really long run on sentence that really needs to be two sentences at least.</p>
<p>'physical traits' to me implies 'they move like people', I think 'physical appearance' might be what you're aiming for? Or alternatively to just say 'humanoid entities that are stationary and made out of roots'.</p>
<p>'stationary in place' is redundant: one implies the other.</p>
<p>I'm not sure what you mean by 'organism above the surface', unless you mean 'identical to non-anomalous flowers'?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The pollen <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">seemed to affect</span><span style="color: green">affects</span> the mind of <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">a</span> subject<span style="color: green">s</span> who enter<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">ed</span> the proximity of the humanoids.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'seemed' is an unnecessary cop out; and the rest is a tense change to make it read better.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>When inhaled the pollen</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;When the pollen is inhaled,&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is unknown what will happen after the symptoms as it is yet to be recorded.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is weird phrasing because it kinda implies the foundation like, were taking notes of someone being affected, and then like&#8230;stopped after a while and then didn't note down what else happened.</p>
<p>&quot;The long term effects of exposure are currently unknown.&quot; would be a better way to phrase this idea.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Similar to the humanoids, SCP-XXXX has an ecosystem made entirely out of carbon-based life and is being inhabitant by an animals that is identical to animals above the cave, however, the animals are made out of the same components as their surroundings, particularly different species of woods, plants, etc.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is another huge run on sentence that really needs broken into smaller parts.<br />
'an ecosystem made entirely out of carbon-based life' is unnecessary and can be cut; same for 'similar to the humanoids': just be like 'SCP-XXXX is inhabited by animals composed of plant matter, which are analogous to non-anomalous animals'. Specifying 'woods, plants, etc.' basically conveys nothing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Footnote 2: It is noted that there’s no soft substance of a human or other animal body, consisting of muscle and fat are present inside of SCP-XXXX.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'It is noted that there's no substance resembling soft tissue, such as muscle and fat, present inside SCP-XXXX'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is speculated that these animals have grown out of nature and started to inhabit the area, however it is yet to be proven.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would cut this because it's just, unnecessarily vague. Perhaps saying 'It is speculated that these animals have evolved naturally' would work but?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>During substantial viewing of SCP-XXXX, it was apparent that the biome inside of SCP-XXXX is contagious to the outside world.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is weird; it doesn't work for me at all and I think it's the way the information is being presented. Something like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The biome within SCP-XXXX is capable of spreading outside the cave system</p>
</blockquote>
<p>would be clearer; but it'd raise questions of why the ConProcs don't really have anything to stop the spread beyond 'arrest stuff leaving the cave'.</p>
<p>It's also unclear what you mean by 'biome' since the only life you've referred to so far is plants making up people/animals, whereas this sounds like you're referring to like&#8230;plant life?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>3 months after SCP-XXXX’s discovery the biome has spread about 7m outside of the cave. Causing the containment of the area to expand along with it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These should be the same sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Currently, there’s no way of stopping it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'there is'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Its skin is olive-brown from sun damage and deteriorating, physically it looks as if it in its mid-teens but its age is currently unknown.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is janky as hell too; something like &quot;Its skin is olive brown from sun damage; physically it appears to be in its mid-teens though the actual age of SCP-XXXX-1 is unknown.&quot; might read better but it feels a little like this should perhaps be two sentences?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>made entirely out of organic material.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'organic material' is entirely too vague: 'plant matter' would be better if that's what you're aiming for? Otherwise the assumption is 'blood and flesh' and then you just have a normal dragon, y'know?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Entities length is unknown.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not a fan of this sentence or the information it conveys: it feels like something like &quot;The entity is estimated to be [30-50m] long&quot; would be clearer; with the size varied depending on your idea of how big this is.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>With indeterminate means, SCP-XXXX-1 can manipulate any carbon-based life for its disposal, this includes causing earthquakes and using it's surroundings as a weapons through telekinesis.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd cut the 'With indeterminate means,' here; it feels like it's better to just say what it can do and not specify how.</p>
<p>Footnote 3 is also unnecessary and I'd cut it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Though it is studied that SCP-XXXX-1, when unresponsive, will still exhibit its anomalous ability and affect the surrounding air, causing asphyxiation on the subject closer to SCP-XXXX-1’s unconscious body.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Consider:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1, when unconscious, will still exhibit anomalous properties which can affect the surrounding air and cause asphyxiation in nearby subjects.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'nearby' feels vague; but I think it's better than specifying it. Though, to be honest, introducing yet more anomalous properties here feels like a mistake: IMO the abilities of -1 need trimmed to one thing it can do.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX and SCP-XXXX-1 were discovered <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">by</span><span style="color: green">during</span> a series of civilian interviews in Altai Tavan Bogd, Mongolia in █/██/2020</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd unredact this date fully: the date isn't sensitive information; particularly not more sensitive than what this SCP can do.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>deployed <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">in</span> to explore the cave and return with the sample</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'with the sample' is still really janky even with a footnote explaining what you mean: I would honestly just say they were deployed to explore the cave and leave it at that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After they had not returned 24 hours later, a recovery team was dispatched to investigate, only the non-organic components of MTF Zeta-9's equipment were found.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would probably cut this? Idk, it feels like opening with 'we didn't find Zeta-9' undercuts a lot of the tension of the log because we know it turns out badly?</p>
<p>Maybe it'd work better noted at the end?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Agent Olson: got it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing capital</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Agent Olson: Currently… nothing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's unclear if Olson means 'We have no ideas about what the cave does' or 'This cave does nothing'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Agent Ouyulan: Then how are we going to travel through this anyway?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There's nothing to indicate there'd be difficulty travelling through this yet.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>any of you hear<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">d</span> anything?</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Shit! why did it get dark? everyone flashlight on!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is weird cos there's been no indication it got dark before this?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The snake lunges at Agent Ouyulan, but she opens fire on the creature, however it doesn't seemed to be affected.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'but' here implies 'the gun fire prevents the lunge', which the 'however it doesn't seem to be affected' directly contradicts.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>During its rampage, its tail hits Agent Olson <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">sending</span><span style="color: green">which sends</span> him flying.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The snake is seen swallowing Agent Zachary whole</p>
</blockquote>
<p>you need to establish the scale of the snake before this: the implication from 'a snake skeleton' is 'snake sized' whereas 'swallows a man whole' implies 'much larger'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Well shit, guess we're alone<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">, are we?</span></p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Yeah, let us stick together. Don't wander off somewhere else alone. Let's get going.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These are highly trained professionals. Wandering off alone is like&#8230;the last thing they should expect the other to do.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The camera activates, the date on the feed <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">tells</span><span style="color: green">indicates</span> its been five hours since the snake attack.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Frantic panting can be heard behind the camera as Agent Olson <span style="color: green">is</span> seen running through <span style="color: green">a</span> narrow tunnel<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">,</span><span style="color: green">with</span> a bright light <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">can be seen in</span><span style="color: green">at</span> the end of it.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The three agents finally reach<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">es</span> a wide space.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'finally' implies the passage of time but cos it's not really shown, it feels weird? Maybe 'After an hour, the three agents reach a wide space' would be better?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>found jack shit and <span style="color: green">n</span>ow we're in a complete<span style="color: green">ly</span> different place.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Agent Olson starts to look around the area, picking up a rock and peddle, feeling the walls of the cave, the camera went static for three minutes and Agent Olson is sitting crossed leg, facing the wall.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Run on sentence</p>
<p>Also I think you mean 'pebble'? But it's weird for Olson to pickup a rock and then not do anything with it: maybe indicate they put it in a sample bag and store it in their rucksack or something?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Is it me or is the air is less timid than when we started?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'timid' is still not the word you're looking for here. I think you want 'thin' maybe?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(a fore)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think this should really be like 'from off-camera' or something?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>drink this<span style="color: green">, it</span> might help.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>It seems like something is messing with frame.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'frame' isn't the right word here: I think maybe 'with the signal' or something but??</p>
<blockquote>
<p>No need <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">for messing</span><span style="color: green">to mess</span> with that thing</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Agent Luna: Umm Cap!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is the only place anyone is referred to as 'Cap': I would use the more familiar designation.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They all are human.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'human' feels strong here; 'They are all human' would be more grammatically correct but 'They all look like people' might be clearer?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The feet of the crowds embedded into the flower field.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Saying this implies 'the feet are suddenly embedded into&#8230;' whereas I think you're really trying to convey that they always were: maybe highlighting someone looking down and noticing it or something would work better?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>it seems like these people were on a run?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The description does not imply this to be the case so it feels like a jarring suggestion.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>//Agent Olson was silent/</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing a / at the end</p>
<blockquote>
<p>facilities in a three-decade <span style="color: green">span</span>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The hyphen is unnecessary too</p>
<blockquote>
<p>You caused thousands of death<span style="color: green">s</span>.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Hence why you're here.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This isn't actually why -1 is here; -1 is here because he's anomalous and the foundation locks up anomalies; they don't really care about regular humans who kill folk.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-CXXX-1: Will you let me go if I answer? I need to go to my people.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'CXXX' should be 'XXXX'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>But I won’t promise you to answer everything.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'But I won't promise I'll answer everything.'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>To be honest I can't quite tell you… I never opened it before.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This implies &quot;-1 doesn't know&quot;, which it's weird for Kent to follow with 'You can tell me'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Kent: Why?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels like it should be &quot;How?&quot; as in &quot;How were your peoples existence threatened&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>When i was a child, there was a two division of belief, and our people belong in none of those division.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure what you mean by 'division of belief'</p>
<p>This whole paragraph feels&#8230;very expositional? In like, a bad way: it's just dumping a lot of info in our lap without really giving us a reason to care about the conflict.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>first generations to <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">have</span><span style="color: green">be</span> in touch with their inner self.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Did you <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">made them</span> turn <span style="color: green">them</span> into a tree like your people?</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
