<p>Thanks for the heads up!<br />
I do have to admit, once i finished the writing i read it about fifty times and every time there’s something that felt out of place or unnecessary but I didn’t know how to approach it. ( got scared to trim it.)</p>
<p>The central core or what i’m really trying to say through the article would be learning who you really are or having peace with you inner conflict and finding power from it. Once the inner peace is achieved no one can really stop you or tell you that your wrong, but the society as a whole always finds a loop hole on the idea. So I guess i didn’t really made it clear.</p>
<p>I’ll make it more clear and try mess with it further.</p>

