															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608733558" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;" >Grigori Karpin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607241912 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2020 08:05</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837757">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">►&nbsp;my&nbsp;detailed&nbsp;thoughts◄</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is to be stored in Containment Area M21 located in 300m underground of the Gobi desert in Mongolia.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>Delete that second “in” (right before 300m)</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is to be held in a 5&#160;m cube made of entirely Tungsten metal, with no gap for organic life to enter.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>Why does it matter that the cube be Five meters in length/widtch/height? What if it were 4.98 meters? Would that invalidate the containment? This is why specific measurements of containment chambers is mostly avoided these days.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>If any entities that reside in SCP-XXXX-1 move from their position, they are to be immediately apprehended and interrogated before being held in a cell with same containment procedure as SCP-CXXX.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest: <em>Entities residing in SCP-XXXX-1 that move from their position, are to be apprehended, interrogated, and remanded to a containment cell under equivalent containment procedures as SCP-XXXX.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>No more than five personnel wearing Hazmat suits, are to enter SCP-XXXX-1 at the same time. Its activity is to be monitored 24/7 and no unauthorized personnel and civilian are to be in the proximity of the area or enter SCP-XXXX-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest: <em>A maximum of five hazmat protected personnel are permitted to enter SCP-XXXX-1 at any given time. Access to SCP-XXXX-1 is restricted to security cleared personnel.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>In the event of a Containment Breach, all on site researchers and personnel are to evacuate immediately or stay in shelter until the MTF Theta-4 (“Gardeners”) arrive at the facility and apprehended the entity.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest: <em>In the event of a containment breach, all on-site personnel are to evacuate or shelter in place until such time as MTF-Theta-4 (“Gardeners”) apprehend the entity.</em></p>
<p><strong>ALSO</strong>: which entity? Clarify</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-CXXX consists of two components: a cave (SCP-XXXX-1) and humanoid protecting it (SCP-XXXX).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest: <em>SCP-XXXX consists of two interrelated anomalies: a cave, designated as SCP-XXXX-1 and a humanoid entity guarding the cave, designated as SCP-XXXX.</em><br />
<strong>ALSO</strong>: I suggest reversing the designations, the Cave could be the XXXX and the humanoid, -1, because it seems the cave is the central anomaly.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is a Hun male, its skin is olive-brown from sunburn and wears an old dark green Hun area deel1 which been ripped and torn, however, SCP-XXXX refused to change it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX has the ability to manifest entities made out of natural components which resemble a Chinese dragon. Entities length is unknown.<br />
So several things, “an old dark green Hun area deel” is confusing… <strong>suggest</strong>: “<em>SCP-XXXX is a Hun male, its skin is olive-brown from sun damage and an deteriorating, dark-green Hun deel that the entity refuses to change.</em>” &amp; <em>I don’t know what “made out of natural components” means in this context, so I would clarify.</em></p>
<p><strong>ALSO</strong>: IS this meant to be two paragraphs? If so, there is no spacing between them.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1 is a cave under abandoned Mining factory, it is measured to be around 6 kilometers deep.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest: <em>a cave under an abandoned mining <strong>facility</strong>, measured to be approximately six kilometers below the surface.</em></p>
<ul>
<li>There is no such thing as a mining factory, change this everywhere… it’s a facility or just a mine.</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>However, how big SCP-XXXX-1 mass is impossible to measure. SCP-XXXX-1 resides a snake-like creature approximately 1 kilometers, maybe even bigger.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest: <em>Exact measurements of SCP-XXXX-1’s dimensions have been impossible due to a large serpentine entity, at least one kilometer in length, that resides within the cave.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>About fifty kilometers down, there is a massive field stretching further from the human eye, filled with stationary humanoids varies in ages, they're made out of natural components, different species of flowers but growing in the same root. The radio cuts off the moment entering SCP-XXXX-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>Fifty kilometers down where? I thought you said the cave was 6&#160;km below the surface? What do you mean? Also this is just really awkwardly written.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>The investigation into SCP-XXXX-1 and its relation with SCP-XXXX is ongoing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Cut this. It’s implied because there’s more to read after it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Due to the unknown nature of SCP-XXXX, MTF-Zeta-9 (Mole Rats) were deployed in to explore the cave and return with the sample</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest: <em>were deployed to explore the cave and return with samples of ___</em><br />
<strong>What samples? Samples of what?</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>After they had not returned 24 hours later, a recovery team was dispatched to investigate, only the non-organic components of MTF Zeta-9's equipment were found.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest: <em>No updates were received from the MTF, and after twenty-four hours, command mobilized a recovery team. Only the team’s equipment was found, missing any components made with non-synthetic materials.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>He continues to cough. His cough becomes more severe as he goes.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>Why is this in bold? Every other bit of narration in the log is in italics, not bold.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>a can of water</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>a <strong>can</strong> of water?</em></p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>You have so many awkward phrases and poorly structured sentences&#8230; I would sit down and really examine your work here, and see if you can't clean it up without myself or another critter to do so.</p>
<p>Additionally, <span style="text-decoration: underline;">all the dialogue is stilted and hard to read</span>. Go through it and say each line aloud, then if it sounds awkward try to make it sound more grounded and believable.</p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Overall</span></strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>There’s a lot of spelling mistakes and failures to capitalize properly in the dialogue.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>There are lots of exclamation marks in the dialogue. Keep in mind that the “!” implies yelling or very energetic vocalizations…</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Don’t do the whole date, team, members and label, over and over in the log. BUT you should include a time stamp, as otherwise I don’t know how much time has passed between the breaks.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>When Olsen starts talking to himself when he’s alone and he doesn’t think command can hear him, it just seems like exposition dump. It doesn’t make sense. People don’t have monologues when they’re by themselves in real life. SO this feels out of place.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>The second collapsible is an interview with XXXX-1, BUT I thought -1 was the Cave? You consistently switch between -1, -2., and plain XXXX… but that’s confusing because before this second log, there’s no mention of a -2</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Audio data of Exploration 02, is very strange. It’s the researcher just speaking into his recording device. BUT why not just have him wear a camera and describe it to us in clinical ways? That would be better.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Honestly, there’s way too much exposition in this. I would trim this down to 50% of its current length, and tighten up the dialogue.</li>
</ul>

							</div>

								
